(* bovnar:retired-path -> 12_bovnar.ebnf *)

(* MOVED: the Bovnar grammar is now doc/12_bovnar.ebnf.

   The documentation set was renumbered and every document gained a two-digit
   prefix. This file is a pointer, not a grammar -- it defines no production and
   will not parse as one.

     Current document:  doc/12_bovnar.ebnf
     Rendered:          https://www.bovnar.io/docs/grammar/
     Raw EBNF:          https://www.bovnar.io/doc/12_bovnar.ebnf

   WHY THIS FILE EXISTS

   The IANA media type registration for text/vnd.bovnar cites this path as the
   published grammar:

     https://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/text/vnd.bovnar

   A registration that has been published cannot be edited in place --
   correcting it means submitting an update and waiting for Expert Review.
   Deleting this file would leave that citation pointing at nothing in the
   meantime, so it stays until the corrected registration is accepted.

   The correction cites https://www.bovnar.io/ paths rather than repository
   ones. Those redirect across renames (the web server 301s every retired
   document path), so the next renumbering will not break the registration
   again.

   Nothing here is normative. Do not cite this file. *)
